  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Cut the cauliflower into small florets. Thinly slice the haloumi. Finely grate the zest of half the lemon, then juice the half. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446859/photos/large/prep_ingredients-33771752874883b155c0ccac93a58ad8.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Marinate cauliflower: Put the garlic, lemon juice, 1 tsp dried oregano and 2 tsp olive oil in a large bowl, then season with salt and pepper. Add the cauliflower and toss to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446860/photos/large/marinate_cauliflower-5ddcfd0211dcdd7f6c2869d43ebbc7e4.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook cauliflower: Heat a large deep frypan over high heat. Cook the cauliflower, tossing, for 2-3 mins until tender and lightly charred. Transfer to a large bowl, add the lemon zest and toss to combine. Wipe the pan clean with paper towel.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446861/photos/large/cook_cauliflower-ae74552e1b57bed25ba67a46f18be770.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm pitas: Heat the same pan over medium-high heat. Cook 2 pita breads, one at a time, for 30 secs each side or until warmed through. Remove from the pan. Heat 2 tsp olive oil in the pan over medium heat. Cook the haloumi for 1 min each side or until golden. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446862/photos/large/warm_pitas-173afbd1bdaeb8cc904f6a04118031e3.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the pitas among plates, then spread with 2 tsp tomato sauce. Top with the spinach leaves, cauliflower and haloumi and drizzle with the yoghurt (see Make it yours). Fold in half and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446863/photos/large/serve_up-50f7f3ca14a7b47becc781275b29c622.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Squeeze a little lemon juice or grate some fresh garlic into the yoghurt to add a flavour twist.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/446864/photos/large/make_it_yours-e9dec887306c64620bc668473489f64e.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
